<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This architecture ensures that <=
strong>revenue-critical features remain responsive</strong> even under netw=
ork stress, while <strong>non-critical features degrade gracefully</strong>=
 to maintain overall system stability. The key insight is that user toleran=
ce for latency varies dramatically based on the feature - users will wait 2=
 seconds for analytics to load, but not for gift feedback.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Th=
is is really impressive thinking! I love how you've considered the business=
 impact in your technical decisions. The graceful degradation strategy is p=
articularly relevant for our global user base with varying network conditio=
ns.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me push you a bit further on=
 the financial accuracy aspect. At TikTok scale, we process millions of gif=
ts per day, and even a 0.1% error rate in optimistic updates could result i=
n significant financial discrepancies. How would you design a system that m=
aintains that instant gratification UX while ensuring we never lose track o=
f a gift transaction, even in edge cases like browser crashes or network fa=
ilures?</p>
<hr>
<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">Part 2: Deep Tec=
hnical Discussion (40 minutes)</h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: That=
's an excellent challenge, and you're absolutely right that <strong>financi=
al accuracy cannot be compromised</strong> even for UX improvements. At Tik=
Tok's scale, even small error rates translate to significant financial impa=
ct and user trust issues. Let me walk through a <strong>comprehensive appro=
ach</strong> that maintains instant gratification while ensuring zero finan=
cial loss:</p>
<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">Idempotent Trans=
action Architecture</h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The foundation is building an <s=
trong>idempotent system</strong> where every gift transaction can be safely=
 retried without double-charging:</p>
