<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">Key Safety Guara=
ntees</h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This architecture provides sever=
al critical guarantees:</p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Zero Financial Loss</st=
rong>: Every transaction is persisted locally before network calls</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Idempotency</strong>: C=
lient-generated UUIDs prevent double-processing</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Auditability</strong>: =
Complete attempt history for every transaction</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Recovery</strong>: Auto=
matic recovery from browser crashes and network failures</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Reconciliation</strong>=
: Periodic validation against server state</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Graceful Degradation</s=
trong>: Offline queue for network outages</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The result is a system that <str=
ong>maintains instant gratification UX</strong> while providing <strong>ban=
k-level financial accuracy</strong> - users see immediate feedback, but eve=
ry cent is tracked and reconciled.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ex=
cellent! Your approach to financial transaction safety is exactly what we n=
eed at TikTok scale. I particularly appreciate how you've thought about off=
line scenarios and reconciliation - those edge cases are often overlooked b=
ut become critical at our volume.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Now let's shift gears to perform=
ance. Our live streams can have 100K+ concurrent viewers, and during major =
events, we've seen spikes to over 1M concurrent users on a single stream. E=
ach user might be receiving 10-20 gift animations per second during peak mo=
ments. How would you architect the frontend to handle this level of real-ti=
me animation performance without dropping frames or crashing browsers?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: That=
's an incredibly challenging performance scenario! <strong>1M concurrent us=
ers with 10-20 animations per second</strong> means we're potentially deali=
ng with <strong>10-20 million animations simultaneously</strong>. This requ=
ires a fundamentally different approach from typical React applications. Le=
t me break down a <strong>performance-first architecture</strong> designed =
specifically for this scale:</p>
<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">Animation Archit=
ecture: Bypassing React for Performance</h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The key insight is that <strong>=
React's reconciliation is the enemy of high-frequency animations</strong>. =
We need a hybrid approach:</p>
