</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The result is a system that main=
tains <strong>60fps performance</strong> even with extreme animation loads =
while gracefully degrading on lower-end devices.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ou=
tstanding! Your canvas-based approach and object pooling strategy shows dee=
p understanding of browser performance optimization. The adaptive quality s=
ystem is particularly clever - it reminds me of how game engines handle LOD=
.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me ask you about state manag=
ement at this scale. With millions of users, real-time gift data, user bala=
nces, stream metadata, and all the complex state we've discussed, how would=
 you architect the global state management? And specifically, how would you=
 handle state synchronization across multiple browser tabs if a user has th=
e same live stream open in different tabs?</p>
