<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This architecture provides sever=
al key benefits for multi-tab synchronization:</p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Leader Election</strong=
>: One tab handles WebSocket connections to reduce server load</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Intelligent Sync</stron=
g>: Only critical state is synchronized between tabs</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Performance Optimizatio=
n</strong>: UI state stays local, financial state syncs immediately</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Graceful Degradation</s=
trong>: Tabs can operate independently if sync fails</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Memory Management</stro=
ng>: Automatic cleanup and caching with TTL</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Conflict Resolution</st=
rong>: Built-in mechanisms for handling state conflicts</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The result is a system that main=
tains <strong>state consistency across tabs</strong> while <strong>minimizi=
ng performance impact</strong> and <strong>reducing server load</strong>.</=
p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Th=
is is really well thought out! I love the leader election pattern and how y=
ou've differentiated between state that needs to be synchronized versus sta=
te that should remain tab-local. The performance optimizations around selec=
tive subscriptions are exactly what we need.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Now let's dive into some code. I=
