<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">Key Design Decis=
ions Explained:</h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>1. Batched Processing</s=
trong>: Instead of updating on every single gift, I batch updates every 100=
ms to prevent excessive re-renders while maintaining near real-time feel.</=
p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>2. Stable Sorting</stron=
g>: The tie-breaking logic ensures consistent ordering even when users have=
 equal gift values, preventing jarring position changes.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>3. Animation Strategy</s=
trong>: Using Framer Motion's layout animations for smooth position changes=
, with separate animations for value updates to provide immediate feedback.=
</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>4. Memory Management</st=
rong>: Only tracking top performers in detail, with cleanup of old data to =
prevent memory leaks during long streams.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>5. Performance Optimizat=
ions</strong>:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Memoized calculations</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Throttled updates for high-freq=
uency scenarios</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Efficient data structures (Map =
for O(1) lookups)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Selective re-rendering</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>6. Edge Case Handling</s=
trong>:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Tied scores with stable ranking=
</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Data validation and sanitizatio=
n</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Error boundaries for graceful f=
ailures</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Empty state handling</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This implementation can handle t=
housands of gifts per minute while maintaining smooth 60fps animations and =
providing an engaging user experience.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ex=
cellent implementation! I'm particularly impressed with your batching strat=
egy and the stable sorting algorithm for handling ties. The error boundary =
and edge case handling shows production-ready thinking.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me ask one final question: G=
iven that this leaderboard will be seen by millions of users globally, how =
would you approach A/B testing different versions of this component? For ex=
ample, testing different animation styles, update frequencies, or even comp=
letely different leaderboard formats. What would be your testing strategy a=
nd how would you measure success?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: Grea=
t question! <strong>A/B testing at TikTok's scale</strong> requires a sophi=
sticated approach that balances <strong>statistical significance</strong>, =
<strong>user experience impact</strong>, and <strong>engineering complexity=
</strong>. Let me design a comprehensive testing strategy:</p>
